exist at least N instances (INS2) of COL2 that have the relation PRED
with INS1, i.e. (PRED INS1 INS2) holds. It allows assertions that
correspond more directly to common database entries, e.g. 'Iran has at
least three oil fields' is represented by a single GAF,
(#$relationInstanceExistsMin #$geographicalSubRegions #$Iran
#$OilField 3), rather than by a rule:  (#$thereExistAtLeast 3 ?OILFIELD
(#$and (#$isa ?OILFIELD #$OilField) (#$geographicalSubRegions #$Iran
?OILFIELD))).  #$relationInstanceExistsMin is thus redundant with a
huge set of commonly-occurring rules.  One must be aware of the
implicit quantification underlying this predicate. ")
)

