  (comment AbstractInformationalThing "The collection of all instances of
abstract information stored or transmitted in some manner, and
representing (to someone potentially at least) something.  Although
abstract information which has propositional content (see
#$PropositionalInformationThing) is an important kind of
#$AbstractInformationalThing, #$AbstractInformationalThing does not *necessarily*
have propositional content; a score for music, or a bit-map, are
examples.  Note that #$AbstractInformationalThing is the abstract, intangible
information, not any particular physical embodiment.  The same
abstract information is often stored in many different physical
#$InformationBearingObjects.  #$AbstractInformationalThing may or may not be
digital; it need not be representable in a particular number of bits.
#$AbstractInformationalThing does not include every abstract #$Intangible or
'Platonic' concept, only that information that represents something
and is (at least potentially) stored or transmitted for that purpose;
thus, the ideal regular icosahedron is not in itself an instance of
#$AbstractInformationalThing.")
)

