non-atomic terms (NATs).  (#$genNatTerm-compoundString FUNC WORD
STRINGS POS CONSTRAINT) means that, for NATs created using the unary
#$ReifiableFunction FUNC, one can deduce (#$compoundString WORD
NEW-STRINGS POS (FUNC ARG)), where NEW-STRINGS combines STRINGS plus
the phrases for ARG that meet CONSTRAINT.  For instance,
(#$genNatTerm-compoundString #$InstrumentPlayingFn #$Play-TheWord
(\"the\") #$Verb #$singular) gives rise to deductions like
(#$compoundString #$Play-TheWord (\"the\" \"piano\") #$Verb
(#$InstrumentPlayingFn #$Piano-Acoustic)).  This allows phrases like
\"play the piano\", \"playing the piano\", and \"played the piano\" to be
both generated and understood.  CONSTRAINT must be an instance of
#$TermPhrasesConstraint.  See also #$genNatTerm-multiWordString,
#$genNatTerm-ArgLast, and #$termPhrases.")
)

