the elements of #$GeopoliticalEntity and #$GeographicalAgent are both #$Agents and #$GeographicalRegions.  This allows us, in most cases, not to reify the #$physicalExtent of the entity, and just state geographic aspects directly about the agent/region combination. Thus, under this microtheory the #$CityOfMiamiFL can be regarded as both an #$Agent -- it can do things like enter into agreements with other cities -- and a #$Place -- it is a patch of ground with certain physical features, boundaries, etc.  See also #$PhysicalGeographyMt, in which #$GeographicalAgents are not also #$GeographicalRegions.

This microtheory is for generic rules about how worlds act that have #$GeographicalAgents which are treated as #$GeographicalRegions.  It should not have any assertions directly related to #$PlanetEarth.  To make assertions specifically about #$PlanetEarth, use the more specific #$WorldGeographyDualistMt")
)

