(1) BEFORE occurs strictly before AFTER; i.e., AFTER starts after BEFORE has ended; i.e., (#$startsAfterEndingOf AFTER BEFORE); and

(2) BEFORE and AFTER are significantly relevant to each other.  This required `relevance' of the two arguments to each other is difficult to formalize but often intuitively clearcut.  Often, e.g., AFTER is caused by BEFORE. For example we would say (#$postEvents TakingAShower001ExitingShower001); we would not say (#$postEvents BolshevikRelvolution DeathOfJohnLennon) since they are not at all relevant to each other.")
)

