(:DIRECTION :FORWARD :MONOTONICITY :DEFAULT :CREATOR Cyc :CREATION-DATE NIL
 :MICROTHEORY BaseKB
 :KIF
  (comment CityGridSectionFn "(#$CityGridSectionFn ST1 ST2 ST3 ST4) denotes the unique,
roughly rectangular urban region (if any) that is completely 
bounded by segments of each of the streets ST1 - ST4.  The relative
order (but not the absolute positions) of the arguments here is 
important: it should be physically possible to circle completely 
the bounded area once by starting along ST1 and making successive 
right-hand turns on ST2, ST3, ST4, and back onto ST1.  The bounded 
area must be part of a region that has a #$GridStreetSystem running 
through it.  To have this function return a given street-bounded 
rectangular city section SECTION, one can fill its arg1 position with 
any of the four streets that borders SECTION, and then continue to 
fill in the remaining argument-places according to the order in which 
one would travel along the other three streets if one were circling 
SECTION in a clockwise fashion (i.e. by making only right-hand turns).
See also #$CitySectionFn and #$CityBlockFn.")
)

