  (comment SKF-40945238 "Rules involving this SKF assert, together with 
other simple rules about links in systems, that nodes on a path in a path 
system are 'discrete'.  In order to say that there are only finitely many 
nodes on a path in any path system, rules involving this SKF are necessary.  
The rule asserted by hand is the following:  

(implies
    (and
     (pathBetweenInSystem ?path ?x ?y ?sys)
     (nodeInSystem ?x ?sys)
     (nodeInSystem ?y ?sys))
    (or
     (linkInSystem ?path ?sys)
     (thereExists ?z
      (and
       (nodeInSystem ?z ?sys)
       (betweenOnPath ?z ?x ?y ?path)
       (linkInSystem (SubPathBetweenFn ?path ?x ?z) ?sys))))).")
)

