  of ACTTYPE from time to time, and would (at least upon 
  reflection) consider such activities important to or 
  distinctive of CULTURE.  These activities might be ones
  commonly engaged in on a regular basis (like praying thrice 
  daily), or might be ones normally engaged in only in particular 
  situations or on special occasions (like joining in group
  singing at parties); all that's essential is that many or most
  participants in the culture do them sometimes.  For a similar 
  predicate that applies to practices distinctive of a culture
  but participated in by a only relatively small, specialized
  subcollection of a its participants, see #$cultureSpecialPractices.
  (In using this predicate it is important to avoid unjustified 
  stereotypes of the culture in question and to refrain from 
  relating the culture to practices that do not accurately 
