  (comment Device-UserPowered "An #$Artifact which has been deliberately designed to perform a
particular function, and which depends upon the physical efforts of
the user to perform that function in part or in whole.  A paradigm
example would be a bicycle.  However, the definition also leaves room
for some counterintuitive cases--combs and forks are also user-powered
devices, on this analysis.  Borderline cases would be devices which
require effort on the part of the user to perform part of the function
but not all of it.  For example, many gas-powered lawnmowers have to be 
pushed by hand, but use an internal combustion engine to impart the necessary velocity to the cutting surfaces.")
)

