  (comment SharedNoteOnPrimaryFunctionOfComputerProgram-CWs "For now, (8/00), it seems that type-level assertions about the #$primaryFunction of an instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW can be made using #$typePrimaryFunction GAFS with #$programUsed or #$programUsed-Generic as the #$Role in arg3. An alternative would be to create primaryFunction-ProgramType, modelled after #$primaryFunction-DeviceType. For example, (primaryFunction-ProgramType PROG-TYPE EVT-TYPE) would mean that a #$primaryFunction of #$ComputerProgram-CWs of type PROG-TYPE is to play the role of #$programUsed-Generic in #$Events of type EVT-TYPE. It does not imply that every instance of EVT-TYPE requires that some instance of PROG-TYPE play the role of #$programUsed-Generic. Rules would be required to represent the relation between the #$primaryFunction of instances of the type-level collections and the #$typePrimaryFunction of these collections. However, until a case is made for creating primaryFunction-ProgramType, #$MWakoff believes that we can reason efficiently with the #$typePrimaryFunction GAFs.")
)

