to a spatial relationship that holds of or among its members.  
(#$arrangementPredicates GROUP PRED) means that either (i) PRED 
is a unary instance of #$SpatialPredicate that holds of all 
#$groupMembers of GROUP or (ii) PRED is an N-ary (for N > 1) 
spatial predicate that \"connects\" all of the members of 
GROUP; that is, for each MEMBER of GROUP, PRED holds among 
MEMBER (in any one of PRED's argument-positions) and some N-1 
members of GROUP.  For example, many arrangements of like 
objects have members that are all #$spatiallyContinuous, and 
proximally-grouped arrangments (such as a grove of trees) are 
likely to be connected by #$near or #$nextToLikeObjects.  
See also #$arrangementNearestPredicates")
)

