(:DIRECTION :FORWARD :MONOTONICITY :DEFAULT :CREATOR Cyc :CREATION-DATE NIL
 :MICROTHEORY BaseKB
 :KIF
  (comment oppositeOnPath-Directly "This predicate relates a customary path such as a 
street to two objects such that one is directly across the 
path from the other.  (#$oppositeOnPath-Directly OBJ1 OBJ2 PATH) 
means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are #$onPath-Alongside opposite sides 
of PATH, and the middle of OBJ1 is directly across PATH from 
some part of OBJ2.  More precisely: a vertical plane passing 
through the volumetric center of OBJ1 and perpendicular to the 
vertical ''plane'' defined by the centerline of PATH (or, 
even more precisely, by the centerline of the segment of PATH 
that OBJ1 is related to by #$alongsidePathSegment) would pass 
through some point in OBJ2.  Note that #$oppositeOnPath-Directly
is _not_ #$symmetricInArgs with respect to its arg1 and arg2 
positions, for if OBJ1 is narrower than OBJ2, it can happen that 
OBJ1 is directly opposite OBJ2 but not vice versa.  For a 
generalization of this predicate that allows the objects to 
be less directly across the path from each other, see 
#$oppositeOnPath-Generally.")
)

