not #$spatiallyIntersects REGION2.  The returned region might 
not be #$spatiallyContinuous, even if REGION1 is.  If 
REGION1 and REGION2 are #$spatiallyDisjoint, the function 
simply returns REGION1.  If REGION1 is a subregion of 
REGION2, the function is undefined.")
)

