  (comment MakingAThreat "A collection of events and a 
subcollection of #$Inform-CommunicationAct. When an #$Agent 
makes a threat, that agent conveys to the #$recipientOfInfo 
that he/she/it wishes to make the content of the threat 
(see #$Threat) true.  The #$recipientOfInfo need not be the 
agent or thing that the threat is directed against.  
Threats are often conditional; i.e., they say 
that if something doesn't come to pass, the agent will 
take an undesirable action: see #$threatens and 
#$threatCoerces.   #$MakingAThreat carries less of a commitment than #$MakingAPromise. Someone who
