  (comment adversarialResponseTo "(#$adversarialResponseTo 
ACT SIT) means that (#$inReactionTo ACT SIT) and that ACT is an adversarial or hostile  response to  SIT.  Roughly  speaking,  ACT is an
adversarial response if (i) the director or performer of ACT 
(AGENT1)
intends ACT to either threaten or harm some interest of some doer
of SIT (AGENT2), and (ii) AGENT1
acts with this intention  towards AGENT2   *because of*   AGENT2's
participation in SIT.   A bit more  formally: in the case of
an adversarial response, AGENT1 has a goal
GOAL1 and AGENT2 has a goal GOAL2 such that AGENT1 believes that AGENT2
is #$responsibleFor SIT and also
believes   that SIT  decreases  the  likelihood  that  GOAL1   will be
realized. This belief causes  AGENT1 to perform  the action ACT, which
#$startsAfterStartingOf  SIT.  AGENT1  believes   that  ACT  decreases  the
likelihood that GOAL2 will be realized.")
)

