in which instances of #$AbstractInformationalThing are collected. #$CollectingInformation 
differs from #$InformationGathering in that instances of the former involve more
than just the transfer of information.  Instances of #$CollectingInformation may
involve actitivites that are not themselves instances of #$InformationTransferEvent.
For example, a military reconnaissance flight might be an instance, or subevent of
an instance, of #$CollectingInformation, but it involves events - such as the motion
of the aircraft - that are not information transfer events.  In addition, 
instances of #$CollectingInformation involve the creation of an instance of
#$InformationBearingObject, which need not be the case for instances of
#$InformationGathering.")
)

