  (comment cultureBeliefs "This predicate relates cultures to the beliefs
  that are characteristic of and important to their participants.  
  (#$cultureBeliefs CULTURE PROP) means that participants in 
  CULTURE (but not participants in all other cultures) tend 
  to believe that PROP is true and would (at least upon
  reflection) consider a belief in PROP to be important
  to or distinctive of CULTURE.  Arguably, every human culture
  has an associated set of beliefs that--taken as a whole--
  serves to distinguish it, more or less, from all other 
  cultures.  This set might include religious beliefs,
  socio-political beliefs, beliefs about the causes of 
  certain things, views on morality, views on how best to
  accomplish certain tasks, etc.  (In using this predicate 
  it is important to avoid unjustified stereotypes of the 
  culture in question and to refrain from attributing to the 
  culture beliefs that do not accurately characterize it.)")
)

