(:DIRECTION :FORWARD :MONOTONICITY :DEFAULT :CREATOR Cyc :CREATION-DATE 135206
 :MICROTHEORY BaseKB
 :KIF
  (comment arrangementNearestObjectTypes "This predicate relates an arrangement of like objects 
to the maximally specific types of object under which all of 
its members fall.  
(#$arrangementNearestObjectTypes GROUP OBJTYPE) means that
(i) OBJTYPE is an instance of #$ExistingObjectType that all 
#$groupMembers of GROUP are instances of and (ii) there is 
no reified instance of #$ExistingObjectType that is a proper 
specialization of OBJTYPE and such that all members of GROUP 
are instances of it.  For example, if the members of GROUP 
are the trees in a date palm grove, then OBJTYPE might be 
#$DatePalm, but would not be the more general #$PalmTree.  
Each instance of #$ArrangementOfLikeObjects should have at 
least one such maximally specific corresponding object type.  
For a more general predicate see #$arrangementObjectTypes.")
)

