  (comment PersianGulfRangeFileMt "This Mt contains heuristic rules for establishing distances between
geographical regions in the vicinity of the Persian Gulf.  Several
simplifying assumptions are used.  We take the diameter of Earth to be
12756 kilometers.  We take the circumference of the Earth to be (2 *
pi * (12756km/2)) = 40074.5 km, and assume that a degree of latitude
in the Persian Gulf region is equal to 1/360th of this, or
approximately 111 kilometers.  We take the circumference of the 20
degree latitude line to be (2 * pi * ((sine 70deg) * (12756km/2))) or
approximately 37657.7 km, and we assume that a degree of longitude in
the region is 1/360th of this, or approximately 105 kilometers.  We
derive linear distances between regions based on their latitude and
longitude, using the Pythagorean theorem.  The simplifying assumptions
we make are significant, and mean that the distances derived in this
file are at best good only to a first approximation.")
)

