(:DIRECTION :FORWARD :MONOTONICITY :DEFAULT :CREATOR Cyc :CREATION-DATE NIL
 :MICROTHEORY BaseKB
 :KIF
  (comment SlotTrendPredicate "Instances of #$SlotTrendPredicate are used to describe trends of some quantity. Some of them make explicit the cause of the trend.  Some make explicit the time period over which those trends occur.   #$SlotTrendPredicates, by definition, use the zeroth argument position to indicate the kind of change.  Net increases, decreases, or no net change are the only kinds of change currently (Feb '98) expressible with these constants.  For a net increase see predicates whose names begin with 'increase', for a net decrease see predicates whose names begin with 'decrease'.  For no net change see #$remainsStableImmediately.  See also #$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates.  A negative exemplar of a #$SlotTrendPredicate is #$quantityChangeFunction.  Although this predicate is useful for representing trends in quantity changes, the kind of change occurring is referenced not by its zeroth argument but by its third argument (a specialization of #$FunctionTheMathematicalType).")
)

