  (comment decreasesCausallyOverPeriod "(#$decreasesCausallyOverPeriod EVENT THING SLOT PERIOD) means that
EVENT causes the value of the predicate SLOT applied to THING to be
lower immediately after (#$STIF q.v.)  PERIOD than it was immediately
before (#$STIB q.v.) PERIOD.  PERIOD must start no earlier than EVENT
starts in order to prevent effects preceeding their causes.  If PERIOD
ends before EVENT, it still must be the case that the value of SLOT
applied to THING must be lower immediately following EVENT than it was
immediately before EVENT.  Like with #$decreasesImmediately, the
decrease need not be monotonic.  This predicate is agnostic as to
whether the decrease occurs during EVENT or after it.  See
#$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates for a map of related predicates.")
)

