 :KIF
  (comment coordinateValuePredicate "(#$coordinateValuePredicate PRED SYS) means that PRED is one of the binary predicates used to describe the location of #$SpatialThings in the #$CoordinateSystem SYS.  The #$arg1Isa of PRED will be #$SpatialThing, and the #$arg2Isa will be either #$Distance or #$AngularDistance (depending on the kind of coordinate system and the specific role of PRED in the system).  In geometric coordinate systems in mathematics, it is points which have coordinate values; spatially extended things are characterized by equations satisfied by the points of which a thing is comprised.  Here we allow spatially extended things to have coordinate values attributed to them directly; so in an assertion of the form (PRED THING VALUE), the #$SpatialThing THING is not necessarily an instance of #$SpacePoint.  However, such an assertion will be true if and only if THING has a part PART such that (PRED PART VALUE); thus there is a natural relation between the coordinate values of an extended spatial thing and those of its unextended parts.")
)

