(:DIRECTION :FORWARD :MONOTONICITY :DEFAULT :CREATOR Cyc :CREATION-DATE 161512
 :MICROTHEORY BaseKB
 :KIF
  (comment ConvPolicyGraphRulesMt "This microtheory gives the rules for using graph theoretic representations of conversation  policies to determine the preconditions for event sequencing and actor roles in a conversation governed  by a policy.  The conversation policies covered by this mt are conversations involving two participants.   In a two agent conversation, the graph representing the ideal sequencing of events can contain weighted  links between the nodes.   The links between types of speech acts can be weighted with a 1 or a 2.  If  the weight of the link is 1, the actors switch roles between acts, i.e., sender of info in the first  act becomes the communication target in the next act and vice-versa.  If the weight between two acts  is 2, then the actors each maintain the same role in instantiations of this act.")
)

