(:DIRECTION :FORWARD :MONOTONICITY :DEFAULT :CREATOR Cyc :CREATION-DATE 143530
 :MICROTHEORY BaseKB
 :KIF
  (comment Compose "(#$Compose BINARYFN UNARYFN1 UNARYFN2) denotes the unary
 function COMP
  that is the \"composition\" of the unary functions UNARYFN1 and UNARYFN2
  with the binary function BINARYFN.  More precisely, COMP maps a given
  argument ARG to a particular thing VALUE if and only if VALUE is the
  result of first applying both UNARYFN1 and UNARYFN2 to ARG, and then 
  applying BINARYFN to those two results.  Symbolically: (COMP ARG) =
  (BINARYFN (UNARYFN1 ARG) (UNARYFN2 ARG)).  The argument-constraints
  on UNARYFN1 and UNARYFN2 must not be disjoint, and their respective
  result-constraints must fall within BINARYFN's arg1 and arg2
  constraints.  For example, (#$Compose #$PlusFn #$SquaredFn #$MinusFn)
  denotes the function that maps a given real number NUM to the result of
  subtracting NUM from its own square (e.g. it maps 5 to 20).")
)

