to individual artifacts that are particularly significant to them.
(#$cultureArtifacts-Significant CULTURE OBJECT) means that OBJECT was 
probably produced within CULTURE, and is highly valued by and meaningful to 
the participants of CULTURE.  Generally speaking, most of the artifacts
associated with a given culture (see #$cultureArtifacts) will not be 
#$cultureArtifacts-Significant.  For example, while the #$StatueOfLiberty 
is certainly one of #$UnitedStatesCulture's #$cultureArtifacts-Significant, 
a souvenir reproduction of the statue is not.  Note that, unlike
#$cultureArtifacts, which takes a _type_ of artifact as its second 
argument, this predicate takes an individual instance of #$Artifact-Generic
in that argument position.")
)

