  (comment relationInstanceExists "(#$relationInstanceExists PRED INS1 COL2) means that there
exists an instance of COL2 (INS2) that has the relation PRED
with INS1, i.e. (PRED INS1 INS2) holds. It allows assertions that
correspond more directly to common database entries, e.g. 'Iran
has an oil field' is represented by a single GAF,
(#$relationInstanceExists #$geographicalSubRegions #$Iran #$OilField),
rather than by a rule:  (#$thereExists ?OIL-FIELD (#$and (#$isa
?OILFIELD #$OilField) (#$geographicalSubRegions #$Iran
?OILFIELD))). #$relationInstanceExists is thus redundant with a
huge set of commonly-occurring rules. One must be aware of the
implicit quantification underlying this predicate. ")
)

