(:DIRECTION :FORWARD :MONOTONICITY :MONOTONIC :CREATOR Cyc :CREATION-DATE NIL
 :MICROTHEORY BaseKB
 :KIF
  (comment relationInstanceExistsCount "(#$relationInstanceExistsCount PRED INS1 COL2 N) means that there
exist exactly N instances (INS2) of COL2 that have the relation PRED
with INS1, i.e. (PRED INS1 INS2) holds. It allows assertions that
correspond more directly to common database entries, e.g. 'Iran has
exactly three oil fields' is represented by a single GAF,
(#$relationInstanceExistsCount #$geographicalSubRegions #$Iran
#$OilField 3), rather than by a rule:  (#$thereExistExactly 3 ?OILFIELD
(#$and (#$isa ?OILFIELD #$OilField) (#$geographicalSubRegions #$Iran
?OILFIELD))).  #$relationInstanceExistsCount is thus redundant with a
huge set of commonly-occurring rules. One must be aware of the
implicit quantification underlying this predicate. ")
)

